    {"id":"zka-note-inner-v1","owner":"ZKA","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"H3(asset_commitment, value, recipient)","collision_analysis":"Fixed arity and typed call boundary distinguish the note preimage in deployed circuits, but the raw transcript is not globally domain-separated.","migration":{"boundary":"zka:note:v2 circuit, note format, VK, tree and settlement identifier","replacement":"H4(DOMAIN_ZKA_NOTE, asset_commitment, value, recipient) with an explicitly versioned outer tag; v1 exits remain accepted"}},
    {"id":"zka-note-outer-v1","owner":"ZKA","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"H2(note_inner_v1, randomness)","collision_analysis":"The first element is the output of the fixed note-inner transcript; this composes a type boundary but does not provide independent prefix separation.","migration":{"boundary":"zka:note:v2 circuit, note format, VK, tree and settlement identifier","replacement":"tagged outer commitment using DOMAIN_ZKA_COMMITMENT; never reinterpret v1 notes or roots"}},
    {"id":"zka-nullifier-outer-v1","owner":"ZKA","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"H2(H2(DOMAIN_ZKA_NULLIFIER, commitment), spending_key)","collision_analysis":"The first outer input is already separated by the registered zka/nullifier tag, so another raw binary transcript cannot collide without first matching that tagged intermediate.","migration":{"boundary":"zka:nullifier:v2 circuit, nullifier tree and VK identifier","replacement":"explicit outer tag in a v2 nullifier profile while retaining permissionless v1 exits"}},
    {"id":"shared-merkle-node-v1","owner":"shared","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"H2(left_child, right_child)","collision_analysis":"Tree type, depth and root registry are external type boundaries; roots from different registries are never interchangeable. Empty roots are depth-pinned by KATs.","migration":{"boundary":"per-tree v2 root scheme plus new root registry and proof/VK identifier","replacement":"typed leaf and node tags per note, nullifier, credential, mandate, revocation and recipient-set tree; old roots remain independently verifiable"}},
    {"id":"zka-context-v1","owner":"ZKA","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"H3(epoch, chain_id, application_id)","collision_analysis":"The output is consumed only in a typed context public-input slot and is never accepted as a note, node or disclosure hash.","migration":{"boundary":"zka:context:v2 public-input and circuit/VK identifier","replacement":"registered zka/context:v2 tag"}},
    {"id":"zka-credential-disclosure-fold-v1","owner":"ZKA","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"iterated H2(accumulator, disclosed_or_zero_attribute)","collision_analysis":"Exactly four fixed positions and a separate mask define the legacy transcript, but its seed is credential_data rather than a domain tag.","migration":{"boundary":"CredNote/disclosure:v2 note type, circuit and VK identifier","replacement":"typed disclosure seed plus position-labelled folds; do not alter v1 credential notes"}},
    {"id":"zka-disclosure-aggregate-v1","owner":"ZKA","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"H2(disclosure_hash_a, disclosure_hash_b)","collision_analysis":"Both inputs are outputs of the fixed four-slot disclosure transcript and the API is typed, but the binary fold has no independent prefix.","migration":{"boundary":"disclosure-aggregation:v2 API/circuit identifier","replacement":"registered aggregation tag and explicit count/order fields"}},
    {"id":"zka-crednote-storage-v1","owner":"ZKA","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"H6(credential_data, context, attr0, attr1, attr2, attr3) used as the value slot of note-v1","collision_analysis":"The result is immediately embedded in the typed CredNote-only note commitment and never exposed as a general disclosure artifact. The transcript commits to every CredNote field because the note hash is the only content constraint applied to a prover-supplied note; an omitted field would be a free witness. Poseidon2 absorbs the message length into the sponge IV, which domain-separates this 6-input encoding from the superseded 2-input H2(credential_data, context) form -- separation of encodings, not a collision-freedom claim.","migration":{"boundary":"CredNote:v2 custom-note type and storage-note hash identifier","replacement":"dedicated credential-storage tag without rewriting v1 notes"}},
    {"id":"zka-multi-input-combine-v1","owner":"ZKA","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"H2(input_commitment_0,input_commitment_1) and H2(input_commitment_2,input_commitment_3)","collision_analysis":"Fixed four-slot circuit layout and public input count provide the legacy boundary; the values are not admitted to Merkle root registries.","migration":{"boundary":"zka_transfer_multi:v2 circuit and VK identifier","replacement":"tagged length-bound input-set fold"}},
    {"id":"zkc-legacy-digest-folds-v1","owner":"ZKC","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"fixed-arity issuer credential digests, attribute folds and jurisdiction leaves","collision_analysis":"Each value is consumed in a credential-type-specific signature or proof input; distinct schemas and issuer verification keys are the external boundary. They are not accepted as roots from other protocols.","migration":{"boundary":"per-credential v2 schema, credential type, circuit and VK identifiers","replacement":"registered credential-type tag followed by position-labelled, length-bound fields"}},
    {"id":"zkc-remaining-predicate-credential-digest-v2","owner":"ZKC","status":"legacy_untagged_exception","transcript":"H4(H4(holder_commitment, credential_id, predicate_type, valid_from), claim_0, claim_1, valid_until) for zkc:cred:{accreditation,source,tax,sanctions}:v2","collision_analysis":"The fixed two-level arity and signed predicate_type distinguish the four remaining-predicate credential forms inside the v7/v8 circuit family, where circuit logic accepts only predicate types 1 through 4 and the issuer policy plus schema/proof/circuit/VK identity supplies the operational type boundary. Neither a credential schema identifier nor a domain tag is hashed, so this transcript is not cryptographically separated from another H4-of-H4 field transcript and must not be accepted outside that typed issuer-verification boundary.","migration":{"boundary":"zkc:cred:{accreditation,source,tax,sanctions}:v3 schemas plus successor remaining-predicate circuit, proof-type and VK identifiers","replacement":"registered credential-type tag followed by a position-labelled, length-bound transcript covering holder_commitment, credential_id, predicate_type, claim_0, claim_1, valid_from and valid_until; retain the v2 digest only for verification under the frozen v7/v8 identities"}},

